Device settings on tv-emu's virtual machine

The display is virtio-gpu: card0, with a connector of the type Virtual named
Virtual-1, where the Pi has card1 and HDMI-A-1. The CPU temperature, the
serial number and the front panel's LED are files of the virtual device,
since the VM has no thermal zone, no serial number in its device tree and no
LED.

Handles are widened again where they come in. RDK's device settings plug-in
keeps them in 32 bits, which loses half of a 64-bit address; see
dsHalWidenHandle() in dshalUtils.h.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [tv-emu virtual machine]

